title: Saved workspaces
tags: GUI
kind: reference
status: proposed
aliases: workspace:save workspace:load workspace:select-default saved-workspace default-workspace
summary: A workspace saved under a name in its repository — its layout alone, or the work in progress too — loaded back here or in a new workspace, one of them chosen as what every new workspace on the repository opens on.

A workspace can be ''saved'' under a name and ''loaded'' back later, after a restart
included. A saved workspace belongs to its repository: it is kept in the repository's
`.metafolder/`, and only a workspace on that repository can save or load it. What
should hold for every repository is the GUI's configuration instead
(`[panel-defaults]`, [[GUI configuration]]).

!! Two kinds: layout and work

|!Kind |!Holds |!For |
|`layout` |the panel type of each slot that shows the workspace, whether it is shown with one panel or two, and the ''layout variables'' — how the panels show things: the columns of the list and their widths, the field `path-ref` opens on, the zoom of each panel… |preferences: how this repository is looked at |
|`work` |everything a `layout` holds, plus the ''work variables'' — what the panels show: the list's query, the file manager's folder, `path-ref`'s scope, the selection |a line of work, taken up again where it was left |

A `work` is a `layout` and more: loading one restores the layout it was saved with.

!! Which variables are saved

A panel type decides for its own variables ([[Workspace variables]]): its `main.js`
exports the list of those that belong to the layout and of those that belong to the
work, by name without the panel's prefix:

```
export const saved = {
  layout: ['columns', 'column-widths', 'sort', 'mode'],
  work: ['query', 'normal-query', 'normal-frozen'],
};
```

The GUI reads it with `import()`, without mounting the panel, so a panel type that was
not opened this session still keeps its variables in the next save. A variable no list
names is never saved. The standard variables are the GUI's: `selected_metarecord`,
`selected_paths`, `selected_metarecords` and `selected_path_ref` are work,
`view.zoom.<panel type>` is layout, and `active_repo`, `metarecords:dirty`,
`pick_request` and `pick_result` are never saved.

What a panel keeps outside the variables — its scroll position, a half-typed draft —
is not saved.

!! The commands

* `workspace:save <layout|work> <name>` saves the focused workspace under that name.
* `workspace:load <here|new> <name>` loads it ([[Panel slots and layout]] for the targets): `here` writes the saved variables into the focused workspace — in one go, as [[workspace:send]] does — and puts its panel types back in the slots; `new` does the same in a new workspace on the repository. A variable the save does not hold is left as it is: loading a `layout` keeps the query.
* `workspace:select-default <name>` makes a saved workspace — of either kind — the repository's default.

The default target of `workspace:load` is `here`; `i` and `b` before its key sequence
choose `here` and `new`, as for every command with targets.

!! The default workspace

When a workspace takes the repository, the repository's default is loaded into it. A
workspace takes a repository when it is created on it — `workspace:new` — or when the
workspace without one takes the repository picked in the [[repos panel]]
([[Workspaces]]). A fork is a copy and does not load it.

Changing the default writes one value: which saved workspace it is. Overwriting that
saved workspace changes what the default opens on.

!! On disk

```
.metafolder/gui/workspaces/<name>.json    one saved workspace
.metafolder/gui/default-workspace         the name of the default
```

Written by the GUI, like the input histories ([[Input history]]): ordinary trackable
content, not `internal/`. A saved workspace carries a `version` field, so that a change
of its format can be recognised and converted ([[Persisted format changes]]):

```
{"version": 1, "kind": "work",
 "slots": {"shown": 2, "left": "metarecord-list", "right": "file"},
 "variables": {"metarecord-list:columns": "…", "metarecord-list:query": "…", …}}
```

A value a panel no longer understands — a column on a field the repository no longer
has — is handled as a stale variable already is: the panel falls back to its default.
A panel type that no longer exists is left out of the slots, and the status bar says so.

!! Open questions

* Workspaces created by a command or a script (`mf.workspace.create`, a script's scratch workspace, a [[value picker|Value picker]]): do they load the default? Proposed: no — they say themselves what they show, and a default would move their panels.
* Saving under a name that exists: replace it, or ask first?
* Unsetting the default, deleting a saved workspace, listing them (the [[workspace-info panel]]?).
* The keys: every single letter is taken; `ctrl+s` for `workspace:save` and `ctrl+o` for `workspace:load here` are free.
